#
# The .m files these depend on, so that changing one rebuilds what
# includes it.
#
# mkdis writes SYS_MODULE=${SYSMODULES:%=$MODDIR/%} and mk treats an
# UNDEFINED variable there as a target it has to make, so "mk install"
# in this directory failed with "don't know how to make 'SYSMODULES'"
# before compiling anything.  It had been that way since the models were
# split into plugins; nothing hit it because nothing in this worktree had
# ever built danby, and a whole-tree "mk install" stops here, which means
# everything after danby in appl/mkfile's DIRS was silently not rebuilt.
#
# BEFORE the include, not after.  mk evaluates assignments in the order it
# reads them, so a SYSMODULES set below the line that includes mkdis is
# set after SYS_MODULE has already been computed from nothing -- which is
# how this was written the first time, and it failed identically.
#
SYSMODULES=\
	danby/atmosphere.m\
	danby/ballistics.m\
	danby/cartpendulum.m\
	danby/chaosmap.m\
	danby/doublependulum.m\
	danby/forcedpendulum.m\
	danby/gravity.m\
	danby/lorenz.m\
	danby/oscillator.m\
	danby/pendulum.m\
